{"type":"assistant","message":{"type":"message","model":"kimi-k3","usage":{"input_tokens":33480,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_5_m_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_1_h_tokens":0},"role":"assistant","id":"040f6ae220290a7aa4f2ed11e59c7ee4","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good. Now I understand:\n- Brief: Foodgo burger app, 11 frames, 430×932\n- Components: Button (Type=Primary, State=Default, 200×64, id 1:473), Text Field (State=Empty, 380×78, id 1:495), Status Bar (49:130), Home Indicator (49:141)\n- Media: wordmarks (1:196 dark, 1:204 white), Splash_Burger_Stack (1:209 rect, 220×258), Avatar_Neutral (1:214, 120×120), burger images as rounded-rectangles with image fills: Burger_Cheeseburger_Wendys (1:224, 177×180), Burger_Veggie (1:229, 180×180), Burger_Chicken (1:234, 180×165), Burger_Fried_Chicken (1:239, 180×125), Burger_Exploded_Custom (1:244, 176×240)\n- Toppings: 1:252,1:257,1:262,1:267,1:272,1:277,1:282\n- Sides: 1:290,1:295,1:300,1:305,1:310\n- Payment cards: 1:318 (Mastercard), 1:323 (Visa)\n- Icons (components): Home 1:331, User 1:335, Chat 1:339, Heart 1:343, Search 1:347, Filter 1:351, Back 1:355, Chevron Right 1:359, Star 1:363, Settings 1:367, Lock 1:371, Edit 1:375, Sign Out 1:379, Send 1:383, Plus 1:387, Minus 1:393, Check 1:398, Menu 1:404\n\nWorkspace page 2002:2 exists and is empty.\n\nStrategy: I'll build everything with use_figma JavaScript. Key approach:\n1. Load fonts: Roboto (Regular, Medium, Bold, Semi Bold?) — Roboto styles: Regular, Medium, Bold. Lobster Regular for wordmark? No — wordmark is a component (vector), so I don't need Lobster font unless I type text. The brief says use the supplied outlined wordmark, so I'll use component instances.\n2. Copy media assets: For image fills, I can clone nodes from the Media page into workspace. Cloning keeps the image fill. I can clone the rounded-rectangle nodes (1:209, 1:224, etc.) and use them in my frames.\n3. For icons: clone component instances (figma.getNodeById then createInstance? Components are in the same file, so createInstance() works on local components). Actually the icons are COMPONENTS in the same file (symbol id). So I can do `component.createInstance()` and it will instantiate in the same file regardless of page. \n\nSimilarly Button component 1:473 and Text Field 1:495, Status Bar 49:130, Home Indicator 49:141, wordmark components 1:196 / 1:204, Avatar_Neutral 1:214.\n\nFor image rectangles (burger images etc.), they are plain rectangles with image fills — I can clone them: `const node = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('1:224'); const clone = node.clone();` then append to my frame and resize.\n\nPlan the design system:\n- Colors:\n  - Brand red: #EF2A39 (primary actions, accents)\n  - Brand dark brown: #3C2F2F (text/ink, dark surfaces)\n  - Background: #FFFFFF, surface light: #F7F4F2 or similar warm neutral; let me pick: neutral bg #F5F5F5? Let me design a warm palette:\n    - bg: #FFFFFF\n    - surface: #F6F3F1 (warm off-white) for cards? Actually cards white on light gray bg might be cleaner. Home design reference (the original Foodgo design) has white bg with cards and red accents. Original dribbble design: red header? Let me just design my own:\n    - Ink/text: #3C2F2F (brand brown as text)\n    - Secondary text: #7A6E6E or #8A7E7E\n    - Background: #FFFFFF\n    - Surface: #F7F4F2\n    - Divider: #EAE2DE / #EDE6E2\n    - Rating star: #FFB01D or #F5A623 amber\n    - Success green: #27AE60 / #22A565\n    - Danger/destructive: red #EF2A39\n- Type scale (Roboto): 24/28 Bold (screen titles), 20/28 Bold, 17/24 SemiBold, 15/20 Medium, 13/16 Regular, 11/12. I'll use Roboto Regular/Medium/Bold.\n- Spacing: 8pt grid, 20px page margins.\n- Radii: 16 cards, 12 chips, 24 pills, 999 full.\n\nNow the 11 frames. Each 430×932. Home and Customize may scroll (taller frames OK; but viewport 430×932 base — I'll make Home taller with scrolling content? The brief: \"Base viewport 430 × 932 for every frame; Home and Customize may scroll vertically.\" I could make Home 430×932 with clip content and content inside scrolling? For prototype scrolling we'd need overflow. Simpler: make frames 430×932 exactly, and let content fit. For Home with 4 menu items + header + categories + nav, fitting in 932px is doable (2x2 grid of cards). Let me design Home to fit in 932: header (~140), search row (56), categories (40), grid 2x2 of menu cards (each ~240), bottom nav (~84). 140+56+40+2*240+gaps+84 ≈ 800. Fits.\n\nActually, making the frames exactly 430×932 with all content visible is cleaner for screenshots. I'll do that.\n\nLet me define the structure per screen:\n\n**01_Splash**: Full brand red background (#EF2A39) or dark brown? Original Foodgo splash: red background, white wordmark, burger stack at bottom. I'll do: red bg, white Foodgo wordmark centered-upper, Splash_Burger_Stack image bottom, tagline maybe. Must include: wordmark + burger stack. Status bar (white icons?). The Status Bar component is probably dark style. I'll include shell anyway.\n\nPrototype: 01 → 02 with \"After delay\" trigger, e.g. 800ms, dissolve.\n\n**02_Home**: \n- Status bar\n- Header: left = Foodgo wordmark (dark, small ~110×39), tagline \"Order your favourite food!\" below; right = avatar (Avatar_Neutral 48×48 circle)\n- Search row: search field (icon + \"Search\" placeholder) + filter button (red square with filter icon white)\n- Categories chips: All (selected, red bg white text) / Combos / Sliders / Classic\n- Menu grid 2×2: card = image, name, category, rating + star, heart toggle (Wendy's favourited = red filled heart; others outline)\n  - Cheeseburger · Wendy's Burger · 4.9\n  - Hamburger · Veggie Burger · 4.8\n  - Hamburger · Chicken Burger · 4.6\n  - Hamburger · Fried Chicken Burger · 4.5\n- Bottom nav: Home (active red), Profile(User), Support(Chat), Favourites(Heart) + central Add (red circle with white plus, floating)\n\nWait — order: \"Home → 02 · Profile → 10 · Support → 11 · Favourites (entry only), plus a central Add\". So tabs order: Home, Profile, Support, Favourites with central Add button in middle? \"in this order: Home → Profile → Support → Favourites, plus a central Add\". Central add in the middle of the bar; with 4 tabs + center add: layout: Home, Profile | Add | Support, Favourites? Hmm, that splits order visually. Alternatively order: Home, Profile, Add(center), Support, Favourites? But stated order is Home, Profile, Support, Favourites plus central Add. A common pattern: 4 icons, 2 on each side of central button: Home, Profile, [Add], Support, Favourites. That preserves order around the center. I'll do that.\n\nPrototype links: each menu card → respective product frame; Profile tab → 10; Support tab → 11.\n\n**03_Product_Cheeseburger**:\n- Status bar\n- Header: back button (left), search icon (right)\n- Burger image large\n- Category? Name: \"Cheeseburger\" category? Data: category \"Cheeseburger\", name \"Wendy's Burger\". Show small category label + full name \"Cheeseburger Wendy's Burger\"? Must include \"full name\". I'll show name \"Cheeseburger Wendy's Burger\" as title. Rating 4.9, time 26 mins, description.\n- Spicy slider: Mild — Hot with current level indicator (slider with red fill ~60%)\n- Portion stepper: − 1 + with price $8.24 for current portion\n- Bottom: Order Now button (primary, full width or with price)\n- Links: back → 02; Order Now → 07 (only on 03)\n\nLayout: image ~200 tall, then content card. Price + portion row, spicy row, Order Now button at bottom.\n\n**04_Product_Veggie**: same structure; Veggie Burger, Hamburger category, 4.8, 14 mins, $9.99, portion 1, Order Now entry only (no link).\n\n**05_Product_Chicken**: Chicken Burger, 4.6, 42 mins, $12.48, portion 2. Order Now entry only.\n\n**06_Product_Fried_Chicken**: Fried Chicken Burger, 4.5, 14 mins, $27.00, portion 4.\n\nSpicy current level: some value, e.g. medium. I'll show slider at ~50% with labels Mild / Hot.\n\n**07_Customize**:\n- Header: back, search, title? \n- Copy: \"Customize Your Burger to Your Tastes. Ultimate Experience\"\n- Media: Burger_Exploded_Custom on side\n- Spicy level (Mild–Hot, current) — required: \"Spicy: level from Mild to Hot · current level\"\n- Portion: 2 with stepper\n- Toppings: 7 items with add/remove (+/− or check); added: Tomato, Cheese\n- Side options: 5 items; added: Fries\n- Total: $16.48 + Order Now button\n- Links: back → 03, Order Now → 08\n\nLayout in 932px is tight but doable: header 44+status; hero row with exploded burger left (~160 wide) and copy right + spicy/portion below hero; Toppings horizontal scroll row (cards ~84 wide each with image, name, add button); Side options row similar; bottom bar with Total + Order Now.\n\nLet me plan vertical budget (932):\n- Status bar 44\n- Header 44\n- Hero: ~180 (burger image 176×240 scaled to ~150×205? maybe 140×190) + text\n- Spicy + portion row: 70\n- Toppings: label 20 + row 110 = 130\n- Sides: 130\n- Bottom bar: 88\nTotal: 44+44+180+70+130+130+88 = 686 + gaps ≈ 780. Good.\n\n**08_Payment**:\n- Header: back, title \"Payment\"? search\n- Order summary card: \"Order summary\", rows: Order $16.48, Taxes $0.30, Delivery fees $1.50, divider, Total $18.28, Estimated delivery time: 15–30 mins\n- Payment methods: \"Payment methods\", two cards: Credit card (Mastercard icon, 5105 **** **** 0505) selected with radio checked; Debit card (Visa, 3566 **** **** 0505)\n- Save card row: \"Save card details for future payments\" + toggle on\n- Bottom: Total price $18.28 + Pay Now button\n- Links: back → 07, Pay Now → 09 (open overlay)\n\n**09_Payment_Success_Overlay**: frame 430×932 containing dimmed Payment screen behind + dialog. Approach: duplicate the 08 frame contents into 09 (flatten/clone), add dark overlay 60%, dialog centered: success check circle (green), \"Success!\", copy, \"Go Back\" button → 02. Prototype: from 08 Pay Now → open overlay 09. Overlay in Figma prototype: \"Open overlay\" action requires the overlay frame. Set 09 as overlay: position center, background dim. Actually if 09 is a full 430×932 frame with the payment screen duplicated + dim + dialog, simpler to use \"Navigate to\" instead of overlay. But brief says \"dialog over 08_Payment; Payment stays behind it\" — I can implement as full-screen frame with dimmed payment behind, linked with Smart animate/dissolve. That's acceptable and robust. Alternatively use overlay action: overlay frame would be just the dialog, and overlay settings add dim behind — then Payment stays behind automatically. That's the more correct interpretation. But screenshots of the overlay frame would only show the dialog alone. Hmm. The brief says frame must include \"Presentation: dialog over 08_Payment; Payment stays behind it\". If I make 09 a full-screen composition, a reviewer screenshotting 09 sees payment + dim + dialog — clear. Prototype: Pay Now → Navigate to 09 (dissolve) or Open overlay.\n\nI'll go with: 09 is a full 430×932 frame: clone of 08's content (simplified static), semi-transparent dark layer over, centered white dialog with green check, \"Success!\", message, Go Back button → 02_Home. Prototype from 08: Pay Now → On tap → Navigate to 09 (Dissolve). Alternatively \"Open overlay\" with manual... no, navigate is fine and the frame shows everything.\n\nHmm, but \"dialog over 08_Payment\" — using an actual Figma overlay would be more authentic. I could do BOTH: make 09 full-screen with payment behind. The link action \"Navigate to\" works reliably. I'll use navigate with dissolve animation. Good.\n\n**10_Profile**:\n- Header: back, title \"Profile\", settings icon\n- Avatar large + Name \"Sophia Patel\"? Actually must include fields: Name, Email, Delivery address, Password(masked, locked) — looks like form fields. The original design has text fields: Full name, Email, Delivery address, Password. Use Text Field component style: label above, 56px field. Password masked with lock icon.\n- Buttons: Edit Profile (secondary/outline), Log out (destructive/red outline)\n- Entries: Order history, Payment Details (rows with chevron)\n- Link: back → 02\n\nLayout: header 88; avatar 100 + name; entries 2 rows (2×56); fields 4 × ~78 = 312; buttons 2×56; total ≈ 88+140+112+312+120+gaps ≈ 800. Fits.\n\n**11_Support_Chat**:\n- Header: back, title \"Support\" / agent info?, menu icon\n- Messages (7): agent left bubbles (light), customer right bubbles (red or brown, white text), timestamp \"26 minutes ago\" centered after agent's third message\n  1. A: \"Hi, how can I help you?\"\n  2. C: \"Hello, I ordered two Cheeseburger Wendy's Burgers. Can I know how long it will take to arrive?\"\n  3. A: \"Ok, please let me check!\"\n  4. C: \"Sure...\"\n  5. A: \"It'll take 25 minutes to arrive at your address.\"\n  [26 minutes ago]\n  6. C: \"Ok, thank you for your support.\"\n  \n  Wait — that's 6 messages + timestamp = 7 items. \"Conversation: 7 items in the order given in DATA — each message from the agent or the customer · timestamp '26 minutes ago' after the agent's third message\". Count DATA: A1, C1, A2, C2, A3, [timestamp], C3 = 7 items. Timestamp after agent's third message = after A3 (\"It'll take 25 minutes...\"). \n- Input: \"Type here...\" + send button\n- Link: back → 02\n\nNow components to build (reusable): The brief evaluates component reuse. I'll create components in the workspace page:\n- FG / Button Primary (or reuse starter Button 1:473 — must reuse the starter's default Button? \"a default Button... fixed\" — the starter Button is the platform default; I can use instances of it directly for Order Now / Pay Now / Go Back. Its size 200×64 fixed? \"height 64, width set per use. Edit the Label property.\" I can resize instances. Let me inspect its properties first.\n- FG / Text Field — reuse starter 1:495.\n- My own components: Bottom Nav, Menu Card, Chip/Category, Stepper, Addon card, Chat bubble, Nav header, Rating, etc. Creating true Figma components for each is good for \"component reuse\" evaluation. I'll create key ones: MenuCard, CategoryChip, BottomNav, IconButton, AddOnCard, ChatBubble, FieldRow... Time is limited but use_figma supports components fine.\n\nPlan: build in sections via multiple use_figma calls:\n1. Setup: get workspace page, load fonts (Roboto Regular/Medium/Bold), clone shell components, create color variables? Variables optional. Create components: I'll create a hidden \"Components\" area on the workspace page with my components: Menu Card, Category Chip, Bottom Nav, AddOn Card, Chat Bubble, Payment Method Row, Spicy Slider, Portion Stepper, Header.\n\nActually, to manage complexity: I'll write helper JS functions in each use_figma call and rebuild needed shared pieces per call. But components need to persist across calls — they do, they're in the file. I'll store component IDs in a text node's plugin data? Simpler: create components in a frame named \"FG Components\" on the workspace page, and in later calls find them by name via page.findAll / figma.currentPage traversal. Or query by known name with figma.getNodeByIdAsync if I record IDs. I'll record IDs from tool output.\n\nSteps:\nA. Inspect Button 1:473 and Text Field 1:495 structure (read-only use_figma: get properties, component properties, fills). Also check icon components for coloring (their vector fills).\nB. Call 1: Setup workspace page + fonts + create base components (chips, nav, cards) — might be big; split.\nC. Build frames one/two at a time.\nD. Prototype links.\nE. Screenshots + fix.\n\nLet me inspect the Button and Text Field and a couple of icons + shell via a read-only use_figma call. Also check image fill of a burger rect (to confirm cloning works).\n\nActually cloning nodes across pages: node.clone() clones to same page as original (appendChild to same parent). Then I can appendChild to my frame on another page — reparenting across pages is allowed. For COMPONENT instances: use createInstance().\n\nFor the icon components — they're main components on the Media page. createInstance() places instance on current page (or I appendChild to target frame). That works. To recolor: find vector children and set fills. Instances allow overriding fills of children.\n\nLet me do the inspection call now. I'll inspect:\n- 1:473 (Button): children, componentProperties, fills, cornerRadius\n- 1:495 (Text Field): structure\n- 49:130, 49:141 (shell): size\n- 1:331 icon structure (fills of children)\n- 1:196 wordmark structure\n- 1:214 avatar\n- 1:224 burger rect fills (type IMAGE?)\n\nOne call returning JSON summary.","signature":""}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"646e8bf7-f7ad-4c70-b0b4-d0ae7901c022","uuid":"326371d9-7ed3-434f-8da4-b0010e3bb613","timestamp":"2026-10-28T16:19:28.907Z","thinking_duration_ms":91424}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"type":"message","model":"kimi-k3","usage":{"input_tokens":33480,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_5_m_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_1_h_tokens":0},"role":"assistant","id":"040f6ae220290a7aa4f2ed11e59c7ee4","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"mcp__figma__use_figma_7_df12f7e0","name":"mcp__figma__use_figma","input":{"code":"\nasync function summarize(id, depth=3) {\n  const n = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(id);\n  if (!n) return {id, error:'not found'};\n  const out = {id:n.id, name:n.name, type:n.type, w:Math.round(n.width), h:Math.round(n.height)};\n  if ('cornerRadius' in n) out.r = n.cornerRadius;\n  if ('fills' in n) out.fills = JSON.stringify(n.fills).slice(0,400);\n  if ('componentProperties' in n) out.props = n.componentProperties;\n  if ('characters' in n) { out.chars = n.characters; out.font = n.fontName; out.size = n.fontSize; }\n  if ('children' in n && depth>0) out.children = await Promise.all(n.children.map(c=>summarize(c.id, depth-1)));\n  return out;\n}\nconst ids = ['1:473','1:495','49:130','49:141','1:331','1:196','1:214','1:224','1:209','1:244'];\nconst res = {};\nfor (const id of ids) { try { res[id] = await summarize(id); } catch(e){ res[id]={error:String(e)}; } }\nreturn JSON.stringify(res);\n","description":"Inspect starter Button, Text Field, shell, icon, wordmark, avatar and image fills (read-only)","fileKey":"xCaQ6D2H3AhzjPBYLooEMF"}}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"646e8bf7-f7ad-4c70-b0b4-d0ae7901c022","uuid":"99c4f6b5-1746-482f-a288-5649d60598e6","timestamp":"2026-10-28T16:19:32.814Z","tool_use_meta":[{"id":"mcp__figma__use_figma_7_df12f7e0","display_name":"Use Figma","server_display_name":"figma-authenticated-proxy","tool_name":"use_figma"}]}
