{"type":"assistant","message":{"type":"message","model":"kimi-k3","usage":{"input_tokens":37670,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_5_m_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_1_h_tokens":0},"role":"assistant","id":"02216ae2209a0a7a047a38983b03e601","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I have what I need:\n\n- Button component (1:473): 200×64, radius 20, red fill, white Roboto SemiBold 18 label \"Order Now\".\n- Text Field (1:495): 380×78 with label \"Email\" + field 56px radius 12 white.\n- Shell: Status Bar 430×44, Home Indicator 430×34, white bg with black marks.\n- Wordmark Dark: 171×60 dark brown vector; White variant 1:204.\n- Avatar_Neutral: 120×120 r24 cream bg + red shapes.\n- Images: rects with IMAGE fills (FIT). I can clone those rects.\n\nCheck remaining image node ids:\n- 1:229 Burger_Veggie, 1:234 Burger_Chicken, 1:239 Burger_Fried_Chicken\n- Toppings: 1:252 Tomato, 1:257 Onions, 1:262 Pickles, 1:267 Bacon, 1:272 Cheese, 1:277 Mushroom, 1:282 Avocado\n- Sides: 1:290 Fries, 1:295 Coleslaw, 1:300 Salad, 1:305 Onion_Rings, 1:310 Mozzarella_Sticks\n- Payment: 1:318 Card_Mastercard, 1:323 Card_Visa\n- Icon components: Home 1:331, User 1:335, Chat 1:339, Heart 1:343, Search 1:347, Filter 1:351, Back 1:355, Chevron Right 1:359, Star 1:363, Settings 1:367, Lock 1:371, Edit 1:375, Sign Out 1:379, Send 1:383, Plus 1:387, Minus 1:393, Check 1:398, Menu 1:404\n- Wordmark White 1:204.\n\nNow design the system:\n\n**Palette**\n- brand.red #EF2A39\n- brand.brown #3C2F2F\n- bg.screen #F5F4F2 (warm off-white) — or white. I'll go #F7F5F3 warm.\n- surface #FFFFFF\n- text.primary #1D1A1A (near-black warm) or use brown as primary text. I'll use brown #3C2F2F as text primary for brand feel, secondary #8A7F7F (warm gray), tertiary #BDB3B3.\n- border #EAE5E4\n- rating amber #FFB930 or #F5A623 — I'll use #FFB320.\n- success #1DB954? better warm-compatible green #2FA05A.\n- mild: green #4CAF50, medium: orange #FF8A00, hot: red #EF2A39 for the spice slider gradient.\n- splash bg: red #EF2A39.\n\n**Type scale (Roboto)**\n- 10/12 caps labels (Medium)\n- 12/16 small (Regular/Medium)\n- 14/20 body (Regular/Medium/SemiBold)\n- 16/22 bodyLarge (SemiBold)\n- 18/24 title3 (SemiBold)\n- 22/28 title2 (Bold)\n- 28/34 title1 (Bold)\n\n**Radius**: 12 (fields), 16 (cards), 20 (buttons), 28 (sheets/dialogs), pill 999.\n\n**Spacing**: 4-base, screen padding 20 (matches 24 in starter? starter used 24 inside components area; screen padding I'll use 20).\n\nNow build components in workspace page (2002:2). I'll create a \"DS\" section frame containing components, then screens.\n\nComponents to create:\n1. `DS / Nav / TabBar` (frame 430×96: 4 tabs + labels + central add button + home indicator included? Keep home indicator separate as starter shell instance; include in each screen directly). TabBar: white surface, top border, 4 items each 24 icon + 10px label; center Add button = red circle 56 with white plus, floating above bar (y offset -20). Current tab red, others gray #8A7F7F. I'll build one component with variant-ish approach: since variants across current tabs are more work, I'll create the component with property Current = Home/Profile/Support/Favourites as component set? Component variants: I can create 4 variants in a component set \"Nav / TabBar\" with property \"Current\". Instances then set props. Let me do that: combineAsVariants of 4 frames. Each 430×88.\n2. `DS / Button / Primary` — copy starter 1:473 into workspace (it becomes a component copy there). Reuse directly for Order Now/Pay Now/Go Back. Also create `DS / Button / Secondary` (white, border, brown text) and `DS / Button / Destructive`? Log out uses Sign Out icon + red text row — not a button. Edit Profile → secondary button. Go Back → primary.\n3. `DS / Chip / Category` variants Selected/Default: pill 36 h, radius 999; selected red bg white text, default white bg brown text border.\n4. `DS / Field / Search`: 56 h white radius 16 with search icon + \"Search\" placeholder. Plus filter button separate: `DS / IconButton / Filter` red square 56 r16 white filter icon.\n5. `DS / Card / MenuItem`: 186×220 white r20 shadow: image top (FIT), category small, name, row rating star + favourite heart.\n6. `DS / Header / Main` (back + search): 44 h row: back button (44×44 white circle/rounded, back icon) + right search icon-button. Actually must-include: back · search. I'll make `DS / IconButton` variants: Back, Search, Settings, Menu, Send? Simpler: one component `DS / IconButton` with variants: Type=Back/Search/Settings/Menu. Plus `DS / AppHeader` composing back+search? Keep header built per screen using IconButton instances; but reuse requirement — header is repeated pattern: `DS / Header / Sub` = back button left, search right, 430 wide, 44+padding. I'll make it a component (frame, not variants) with both icon buttons as instances inside.\n7. `DS / Stepper / Portion`: minus circle btn, number, plus circle btn (red filled, white icons; minus white bordered).\n8. `DS / Slider / Spicy`: labels Mild/Hot + track with 3 stops and thumb at current. States differ per screen: Cheeseburger current Mild? Brief: \"current level\" unspecified per burger → I decide: Cheeseburger=Mild, Veggie=Mild? To demonstrate states vary: Cheeseburger: Mild, Veggie: Mild, Chicken: Medium, Fried Chicken: Hot. Component variants Level=Mild/Medium/Hot.\n9. `DS / Addon / Chip`: topping card 72w with image + label + add/remove state (variants Added/Default). Added: red border + check badge; default: gray border + plus.\n10. `DS / Row / PaymentMethod`: variants Selected/Default with card image, name, number, radio.\n11. `DS / Row / ProfileMenu`: label + chevron (Order history, Payment Details).\n12. `DS / Toggle / On`: for save card.\n13. `DS / Bubble / Chat`: variants Agent/Customer.\n14. `DS / Field / Profile`: locked field with label, value, lock icon (reuse starter TextField structure? The starter Text Field is for empty state; Profile fields show values. I'll build `DS / Field / Profile` with label+value+lock).\n15. `DS / Badge / Rating`: star + value? inline in card.\n\nAlso home indicator + status bar: use starter components instances (clone into workspace? They're components in another page; I can create instances directly via createInstanceAsync after finding them — instances must be placed in current page; instances of components from same file are fine).\n\nApproach: use `component.createInstance()`? In plugin: `const inst = comp.createInstance();` then `page.appendChild(inst)` or parent.appendChild(inst). Components from other pages can be instantiated. But instances of library-local components are fine.\n\nHowever, note: creating instances requires the component; images rects can be cloned directly (they're plain rectangles with image fills) — clone keeps image.\n\nPlan the build sequence:\n\nStep A: setup — switch to workspace page, create DS container frame \"· Design System\" at (0,0), screens start at y 0, x from 600. Actually let me place DS at x=0 and screens starting x=700, spaced 470 apart, y=0. 11 frames wide = 700 + 11*500 ≈ 6200 wide. Fine.\n\nStep B: create components:\n- IconButton component set? Variants via combineAsVariants need components with same name pattern \"Type=Back\" etc. I'll create 4 separate small components then combine into set. Might be simpler: create single component `IconButton / Back` etc as individual components (not variants) — acceptable reuse. But \"state design\" evaluated... states = selected etc. Variants show state design nicely for Chip, Slider, Addon, PaymentMethod, TabBar, Bubble, Button (Default/Pressed/Disabled?), maybe show Pressed/Disabled variants for button too — could add. Keep scope sane: variants where states matter: Category chip (Selected/Default), TabBar (Current=...), Slider (Level), Addon chip (Added/Default), Payment row (Selected/Default), Bubble (Agent/Customer), Button (Primary/Default is starter; I'll add variants Pressed and Disabled in my own component set copy). Heart favourite toggle on card: within card component make variant Favourited=True/False.\n\nLet me also reuse starter Button: copy component into workspace DS frame and extend into variant set with Pressed + Disabled + maybe Secondary. Component property: Variant=Primary/Secondary, State=Default/Pressed/Disabled? 2D variants = 6 frames. Maybe simpler: Variant=Primary/Secondary/Ghost? Keep: my own `DS / Button` set with Variant=Primary|Secondary|Destructive(text?) — I'll do Primary, Secondary; each with State Default/Pressed/Disabled → 6 variants. That demonstrates state design. Log out is a menu row with icon, not a button.\n\nField: starter TextField State=Empty; my own `DS / Field` variants State=Empty (copy starter)/Filled/Focused/Disabled? Profile uses filled+locked. Search field separate component. Keep: `DS / Field` set: State=Empty (clone starter), State=Filled (value dark text), State=Focused (red border), State=Disabled (gray bg, lock icon). Use Disabled for password (masked, locked) and Filled for name/email/address on profile. Actually brief: password masked + locked. Use Disabled variant with lock icon.\n\nGiven message size limits, I'll build in several use_figma calls:\n\nCall 1: setup page, load fonts, create DS root frame, copy starter Button + TextField into workspace DS frame, build Button variant set (add Secondary/Pressed/Disabled by cloning the copied component and modifying), build Field variants. Return IDs.\n\nCloning a component: comp.clone() stays on same page; then move to workspace page via wsPage.appendChild(clone). Components on different pages fine.\n\nBut note: starter Button clone keeps label text node with same font (Roboto SemiBold — need fonts loaded before editing text; cloning doesn't require loading unless I change characters. I'll load fonts first anyway: Roboto Regular/Medium/SemiBold/Bold, Inter Semi Bold (status bar text untouched — no need), Lobster? Wordmark is vector