stroke; image ~52×52 FIT top y10 center; label 11 Medium center below; state icon: circle 20 at top-right corner (x=58,y=6): default: white stroke LINE, plus 12 BROWN? added: RED fill, check white 12. Combine variants Added=False/True. Label chars overridden per instance.\n\n**PaymentRow**: 390×72 white r16 stroke: Selected → stroke RED 1.5 + radio red; Default → stroke LINE. Contents: logo frame 48×32 left x16 (image placed per instance — but component variants share children; images differ per instance: place image rect as child cloned into instance (appendChild to instance not allowed!). Instances can't have appended children. So include both images in component with visibility toggled? Instance overrides allow visibility toggling! Component contains both Card_Mastercard clone and Card_Visa clone; per instance set visibility. And texts overridden. Radio: outer circle 20 stroke + inner dot 10 (visible only selected). Combine variants Selected=False/True toggling stroke + inner dot visibility.\n\nClones of image rects inside component: fine (plain rects).\n\n**Toggle**: 48×28 r999: On: RED fill, knob white 22 at right. Off: #E9E3E1, knob left. Variants State=On/Off. Use On.\n\n**Bubble**: variants From=Agent/Customer. Auto-layout hug: pad 16/12, maxW? auto-layout with hug: width hugs text (text fixed width when wrap). Agent: white fill, stroke LINE, r18 with bottom-left 4? cornerRadii supported: set bottom-left small. Customer: RED fill white text, bottom-right small. I'll set text as child with w280 fixed? Then all bubbles same width — ugly for short msgs. Instead: component with text autoResize W&H, hug; instances with long text: set instance text to fixed width via override? Text autoResize override on instances is allowed? Setting textAutoResize on instance text is allowed? Instance sublayer property overrides limited to certain props; autoResize is overridable? Not sure. Safer: build bubbles inline on the screen (not component), but then \"component reuse\" less. Alternative: two components: Bubble/Agent, Bubble/Customer as separate components (not variants), text inside autoResize W&H; for long customer message set component text width fixed 280 with height auto — then all instances of that component 280 wide. Customer has 3 messages: long, short \"Sure...\", medium \"Ok, thank you...\". Mixed widths needed.\n\nPragmatic: make Bubble a variant component where text is child; in instances I override chars; short texts hug. For the long C1 message, I need wrap → fixed width. I can create the component with text autoResize HEIGHT and width 280 → all instances 280 wide. Short messages 280-wide bubbles look padded but acceptable? Meh.\n\nBetter: skip bubble component; build inline with manual measurement (I'll measure text width via creating text with W&H then reading width, then resizing frame accordingly — all doable in code). Reuse still demonstrated by many other components. But chat is 7 repeated patterns... I'll do the manual-measure approach but ALSO create the Bubble component set for reuse credit? Over-engineering. Decision: build bubbles inline (helper function), no component. Fine.\n\n**TabBar**: 430×88: bg white top stroke LINE; 4 tab cells each ~86 wide at y8: icon 24 + label 10 Medium; current red, others FAINT/SUB. Center Add: circle 56 RED at (187, -20) with white plus 24 + shadow; bar itself white. To have the add button overflow above bar, component height 88 includes overflow visible (clipContent false). Variants Current=Home/Profile/Support/Favourites: set icon+label colors accordingly. Tab icons: Home/User/Chat/Heart instances; labels Home/Profile/Support/Favourites.\n\nReactions inside variants: Home cell → 02, Profile cell → 10, Support cell → 11. Favourites & Add: no link (entry only).\n\n**Header/Sub** component: 430×44(+y?) Actually just row: back IconButton (instance of IconButton Type=Back) x20, search right x366. As component 430×44 transparent. Reuse on 03-08. Profile uses back+settings → separate arrangement; chat back+menu. So Header/Sub used on 6 frames. \n\nAlso **RatingBadge**? inline.\n\nSuccessDialog component: 320×340 as described; instance used in 09.\n\nOK calls:\n\nCall 1: page switch + fonts + DS frame + clone starter comps + Button set + Field set. Return ids JSON.\nCall 2: IconButton set, Category chip set, SearchField, MenuCard set, Stepper, Slider set, Toggle set, AddonChip set, PaymentRow set, TabBar set, HeaderSub component, SuccessDialog. Return ids.\nCall 3: 01_Splash + 02_Home.\nCall 4: 03 + 04 (product builder fn).\nCall 5: 05 + 06.\nCall 6: 07_Customize.\nCall 7: 08_Payment.\nCall 8: 09 overlay + 10 Profile.\nCall 9: 11 Chat.\nCall 10: reactions wiring + flowStartingPoints? For prototype start: set 01 as flow start? Nice: figma.currentPage.flowStartingPoints = [{nodeId: splash, name:'Foodgo'}]. \nCalls 11+: screenshots + fixes.\n\nWatch message sizes: keep each call focused; return only essential ids (map of component ids + variant info + screen frame ids).\n\nCareful with combineAsVariants: parent must contain components; names \"Prop=Val, Prop=Val\". After combine, resulting component set id. Instance creation from set: `set.createInstance()` gives instance of default (first) variant; then set `inst.setProperties({...})`? For variant instances: instance.setProperties({'Variant':'Secondary'})? The API: instance.setProperties? There's `instance.setProperties()` on InstanceNode for component properties — yes exists. Variant switching via setProperties({\"Variant\":\"Secondary\",\"State\":\"Disabled\"}) — property names as defined.\n\nAfter combineAsVariants, the component set gets componentProperties with variant options.\n\nFonts loading list:\n- {family:'Roboto',style:'Regular'},{...'Medium'},{...'SemiBold'},{...'Bold'}\n- maybe Inter Semi Bold not needed.\n\nText creation helper:\nasync function T(parent, {chars, x,y,w, size, style='Regular', color, ls, lh, align, caps, autoH}) — create, set font, chars, positions, textAutoResize.\n\nSince every text edit needs loaded font, helper loads font each time (cheap after first).\n\nShadows: effects on frames allowed: [{type:'DROP_SHADOW', color:{r,g,b,a}, offset:{x,y}, radius, spread, visible, blendMode:'NORMAL', showShadowBehindNode? not needed}].\n\ncornerRadii per-corner: use `node.bottomLeftRadius` etc. — rectangles & frames support individual corner radii props (topLeftRadius etc.). Yes.\n\nIcon recolor helper:\nfunction paintIcon(node, c){ if(node.type==='VECTOR'||'BOOLEAN_OPERATION'||'ELLIPSE'||'RECTANGLE'||'POLYGON'||'STAR'||'LINE'){ try{node.fills=[{type:'SOLID',color:c}]; if(node.strokes?.length) node.strokes=[{type:'SOLID',color:c}]; }catch(e){} } if('children' in node) node.children.forEach(k=>paintIcon(k,c)); }\nCareful: Avatar recolor no — avatar keep as-is.\n\nStatus bar recolor for splash: override children fills black→white: paintIcon-like traversal but includes TEXT nodes (fills). And status bar bg: inst.fills = red. Home indicator: bar rect white; bg fill transparent? give red.\n\nInstance fill override: allowed on instance itself (fills overridable).\n\nImage clones: need original rect nodes (on Media page). clone() then parent.appendChild. Keep scaleMode FIT; set size.\n\nFor avatar scaling: resize(40,40).\n\nWordmark Dark: resize 110→ h = 110*60/171 = 38.6.\n\nLet me also decide DS frame layout: x=0 width 640, content flows vertically; components placed with labels. Height ~ 3000. Fine, set as we go (use a cursor y).\n\nAlso nice: paint styles for palette. Quick: figma.createPaintStyle() name 'Brand/Red' etc. Add in call 1.\n\nLet me write Call 1 code.\n\nAlso note: figma.setCurrentPageAsync required.\n\nOne more consideration — createInstance on components that live on other pages: allowed; instance initially appended to component's parent? docs: createInstance creates instance as sibling? It appends to the same page? To be safe, immediately appendChild to target parent.\n\nTesting component property names post-combine: return set.componentPropertyDefinitions.\n\nEdge: combineAsVariants requires all variant components to have same number of props pattern; my clones renamed accordingly before combining.\n\nFor Button variants: starter has name \"Type=Primary, State=Default\" already! Its props: variant-style name. I can clone it twice as Primary/Pressed & Primary/Disabled, plus create secondary trio from another clone (fill white, stroke, label brown). Names: keep \"Type=Primary, State=Default\", \"Type=Primary, State=Pressed\", etc. Combine 6 → set \"Button\". Property \"Type\" and \"State\". Good.\n\nText inside: change label chars per instance (\"Order Now\",\"Pay Now\",\"Go Back\",\"Edit Profile\"). Default starter label \"Order Now\".\n\nField set: starter \"State=Empty\" name already pattern. Clone → \"State=Filled\" (value color INK, chars \"Value\"→ keep \"name@example.com\"? set chars \"Value\"). \"State=Focused\": field stroke red 1.5, value color INK. \"State=Disabled\": field fill #F1EDEA, value FAINT, add lock icon instance at right (icon 1:371, 18px, FAINT). Combine 4 → \"Text Field\".\n\nInstance usage on profile: override Label chars + Value chars.\n\nReturn JSON ids in call1: {btnSet, fieldSet, dsFrame, styles}.\n\nSizing: keep code under 50k chars — comfortably fine.\n\nNow write call 1.","signature":""}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"646e8bf7-f7ad-4c70-b0b4-d0ae7901c022","uuid":"a6c6090a-765b-4a44-82f3-97a1ad295b08","timestamp":"2026-10-28T16:24:13.224Z","thinking_duration_ms":271999}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"type":"message","model":"kimi-k3","usage":{"input_tokens":37670,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_5_m_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_1_h_tokens":0},"role":"assistant","id":"02216ae2209a0a7a047a38983b03e601","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have all the info I need. Now I'll set up the workspace: switch to the 03 · Workspace page, load fonts, create a design-system frame, copy the starter Button/Text Field components in, extend them into variant sets, and register color styles."}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"646e8bf7-f7ad-4c70-b0b4-d0ae7901c022","uuid":"ebe364b5-c227-46a1-a69f-5466fc05d0ce","timestamp":"2026-10-28T16:24:15.036Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"type":"message","model":"kimi-k3","usage":{"input_tokens":37670,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_5_m_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_1_h_tokens":0},"role":"assistant","id":"02216ae2209a0a7a047a38983b03e601","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"mcp__figma__use_figma_8_be4767dc","name":"mcp__figma__use_figma","input":{"code":"\nconst ws = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('2002:2');\nawait figma.setCurrentPageAsync(ws);\nconst fonts = ['Regular','Medium','SemiBold','Bold'].map(s=>({family:'Roboto',style:s}));\nfor (const f of fonts) await figma.loadFontAsync(f);\n\nconst RED={r:0.937,g:0.165,b:0.224}, REDD={r:0.82,g:0.13,b:0.19};\nconst BROWN={r:0.235,g:0.184,b:0.184};\nconst BG={r:0.969,g:0.961,b:0.953};\nconst SUB={r:0.545,g:0.498,b:0.498};\nconst FAINT={r:0.741,g:0.702,b:0.702};\nconst LINE={r:0.925,g:0.906,b:0.898};\nconst DISABLED_BG={r:0.945,g:0.929,b:0.918};\nconst WHITE={r:1,g:1,b:1};\n\n// color styles\nasync function style(name,c){ const s=figma.createPaintStyle(); s.name=name; s.paints=[{type:'SOLID',color:c}]; return s.id; }\nconst styleIds={};\nstyleIds['Brand/Red']=await style('Brand/Red',RED);\nstyleIds['Brand/Dark Brown']=await style('Brand/Dark Brown',BROWN);\nstyleIds['Surface/Screen']=await style('Surface/Screen',BG);\nstyleIds['Text/Secondary']=await style('Text/Secondary',SUB);\nstyleIds['Border/Default']=await style('Border/Default',LINE);\n\n// DS frame\nconst ds = figma.createFrame();\nds.name='🧩 Design System — Foodgo';\nds.x=0; ds.y=0; ds.resize(640, 2400);\nds.fills=[{type:'SOLID',color:{r:0.985,g:0.98,b:0.975}}];\nds.clipsContent=false;\n\nasync function T(parent,chars,{x=0,y=0,w,size=14,style='Regular',color=BROWN,ls,lh,align}={}){\n  const t=figma.createText();\n  t.fontName={family:'Roboto',style};\n  t.characters=chars;\n  t.fontSize=size; t.fills=[{type:'SOLID',color}];\n  if(ls!==undefined) t.letterSpacing={unit:'PIXELS',value:ls};\n  if(lh!==undefined) t.lineHeight={unit:'PIXELS',value:lh};\n  if(align) t.textAlignHorizontal=align;\n  if(w){ t.textAutoResize='HEIGHT'; t.resize(w,t.height);} else t.textAutoResize='WIDTH_AND_HEIGHT';\n  t.x=x; t.y=y; parent.appendChild(t); return t;\n}\nfunction label(txt,y){ return T(ds,txt,{x:24,y,size:13,style:'SemiBold',color:SUB,ls:1.2}); }\n\n// ---- Button variants ----\nlabel('BUTTON · Type / State',24);\nconst btnSrc = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('1:473');\nconst bP = btnSrc.clone(); ds.appendChild(bP); bP.x=24; bP.y=60;\nfunction btnFrom(src,name){ const c=src.clone(); ds.appendChild(c); c.name=name; return c; }\nconst bPp=btnFrom(bP,'Type=Primary, State=Pressed');\nbPp.fills=[{type:'SOLID',color:REDD}];\nconst bPd=btnFrom(bP,'Type=Primary, State=Disabled');\nbPd.fills=[{type:'SOLID',color:DISABLED_BG}];\nbPd.findOne(n=>n.type==='TEXT').fills=[{type:'SOLID',color:FAINT}];\nconst bS=btnFrom(bP,'Type=Secondary, State=Default');\nbS.fills=[{type:'SOLID',color:WHITE}]; bS.strokes=[{type:'SOLID',color:BROWN}]; bS.strokeWeight=1.5;\nbS.findOne(n=>n.type==='TEXT').fills=[{type:'SOLID',color:BROWN}];\nconst bSp=btnFrom(bS,'Type=Secondary, State=Pressed');\nbSp.fills=[{type:'SOLID',color:{r:0.955,g:0.94,b:0.93}}];\nconst bSd=btnFrom(bS,'Type=Secondary, State=Disabled');\nbSd.strokes=[{type:'SOLID',color:LINE}];\nbSd.findOne(n=>n.type==='TEXT').fills=[{type:'SOLID',color:FAINT}];\nconst btnSet = figma.combineAsVariants([bP,bPp,bPd,bS,bSp,bSd], ds);\nbtnSet.name='DS / Button'; btnSet.x=24; btnSet.y=60; btnSet.itemSpacing=16;\n\n// ---- Text Field variants ----\nlabel('TEXT FIELD · State', 300);\nconst fldSrc = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('1:495');\nconst fE = fldSrc.clone(); ds.appendChild(fE); fE.x=24; fE.y=336;\nconst fieldOf = c => c.findOne(n=>n.name==='Field');\nconst valueOf = c => c.findOne(n=>n.name==='Value');\nconst fF = fE.clone(); ds.appendChild(fF); fF.name='State=Filled';\nvalueOf(fF).characters='Sophia Patel'; valueOf(fF).fills=[{type:'SOLID',color:BROWN}];\nconst fFo = fF.clone(); ds.appendChild(fFo); fFo.name='State=Focused';\nfieldOf(fFo).strokes=[{type:'SOLID',color:RED}]; fieldOf(fFo).strokeWeight=1.5; fieldOf(fFo).strokeAlign='INSIDE';\nconst fD = fF.clone(); ds.appendChild(fD); fD.name='State=Disabled';\nfieldOf(fD).fills=[{type:'SOLID',color:DISABLED_BG}];\nvalueOf(fD).characters='••••••••'; valueOf(fD).fills=[{type:'SOLID',color:FAINT}];\nconst lockSrc = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('1:371');\nconst lock = lockSrc.createInstance(); fieldOf(fD).appendChild(lock);\nlock.resize(18,18); lock.x=380-16-18; lock.y=56/2-9;\n(function paint(n){ if(['VECTOR','ELLIPSE','RECTANGLE','BOOLEAN_OPERATION','POLYGON','STAR','LINE'].includes(n.type)){try{n.fills=[{type:'SOLID',color:FAINT}]; if(n.strokes&&n.strokes.length)n.strokes=[{type:'SOLID',color:FAINT}];}catch(e){}} if('children'in n) n.children.forEach(paint); })(lock);\nconst fldSet = figma.combineAsVariants([fE,fF,fFo,fD], ds);\nfldSet.name='DS / Text Field'; fldSet.x=24; fldSet.y=336; fldSet.itemSpacing=20;\n\nreturn JSON.stringify({btnSet:btnSet.id, fldSet:fldSet.id, ds:ds.id, styleIds});\n","description":"Set up workspace page, fonts, color styles, DS frame; build Button + Text Field variant sets from starter components","fileKey":"xCaQ6D2H3AhzjPBYLooEMF"}}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"646e8bf7-f7ad-4c70-b0b4-d0ae7901c022","uuid":"f71f02d3-a584-456d-a9ed-c3e3222df698","timestamp":"2026-10-28T16:24:50.054Z","tool_use_meta":[{"id":"mcp__figma__use_figma_8_be4767dc","display_name":"Use Figma","server_display_name":"figma-authenticated-proxy","tool_name":"use_figma"}]}
